Step 1 — Data Source (Excel)
An Excel file will store:

Default username and password (always present in the first row).

List of orders and their expected vs. actual quantities from invoices.

Step 2 — Script Reads Excel
Python (or another scripting tool) opens the Excel file.

Reads:

Username/password → For SAP login.

Order list → For checking and updating in SAP.

Step 3 — Launch SAP GUI and Login
The script opens the SAP Logon application.

Selects the correct SAP system (e.g., PRD or DEV).

Fills username and password from Excel.

Logs in automatically.

Step 4 — Navigate in SAP
Script navigates through the required SAP transaction codes (T-codes). Example:

/nME22N → Change Purchase Order.

Selects the Purchase Order number from our Excel list.

Step 5 — Check and Update Quantities
Script reads current quantity in SAP.

Compares with Excel’s actual quantity.

If mismatch → updates the SAP entry.

Step 6 — Save and Logout
After all updates, the script saves changes in SAP.

Logs out of SAP automatically.

